	^ 'Testing strategy (99 tests, all green):
- HSKTestTrie (TestCase, 10): black-box trie. Definitions after registerWord:definition:; multiple definitions stay together; two-char word => depth 3; streamDefinitions: over 我吃蛋糕 answers 我, 吃, 蛋糕; missing word runs the ifNone: block; empty trie depth 1; definitionsFor: raises Error on a missing word; the registered word is stored in the node answered by the stream; unregistered characters become unknown nodes (their word prints as H(龺)); words sharing a prefix (我 vs 我们) are distinguished (depth 3).
- SRSTestCase (TestCase, abstract): test fixtures for the SRS suites: aLockedKnownContent, aKnownContent, aKnownContentWithSuccesses: (and on:), a fixed reviewDate for deterministic date arithmetic, and collectAnnouncementsOf:during: to eavesdrop announcements. Class side isAbstract. Its own suite run includes the three sub-suites.
- SRSSchedulingTest (8): a locked content is never reviewed (even after 13 successes at maximal level or +7000 days); a content starts locked and unlock flips isLocked/isUnlocked; a new unlocked content has to be reviewed immediately; a successful review postpones the next one (boundary 25 s); the next review happens only when the rate expires (25 s, then 2 min); nextReviewDate is reviewDate + rate of the level; a failed review floors the level to 1 and schedules an immediate new review; a maximal level content (12) is re-reviewed only after 1000 days.
- SRSSkillsTest (7): the same skill tag reuses its SRSKnowledgeLevel; each tag owns its level (skills dictionary structure); a fresh content answers SRSKnowledgeLevel zero (level 1, not interned); overAllLevel is the minimum of the skill levels (identity); increase is capped at rateTable size (12); giveUp never drops below level 1 and decrements two levels per failure.
- SRSAnnouncingTest (8): a successful review announces SRSLevelIncreased and SRSLevelUp (with levelObject, oldLevel and currentDate); a failed review announces only SRSLevelDecreased; a nil announcer is safe; 13 successes announce 13 increases and 13 level ups (documenting that SRSKnowledgeLevel max tracking is unfinished); a failed review is relayed through the SRSUser session announcer (a successful one triggers SRSUser levelup, which breaks on the unfinished SRSGoal); knowledge is interned per session (two equal HSKStrings give the same SRSKnownContent); SRSUser current is a resettable singleton.
- HSKDomainTest (26), black-box on the current state: HSKCharacter: defaults (frequency 4000, wordsAmount 0, seven lazily interned Set collections), equality and hash on traditional+definition, ordering by traditional character, mark:/module/setupModule with interned modules, radical distances (root 0, radical root 1, else 2), hasError flag with HSK(我) printing, phoneticDistance (3 between corpus 有 and a constructed ni3 你, -1 with itself) and pronouncedLike: on shared pinyin.
- HSKDomainTest, HSKString (8): built through the corpus (爱 -> traditional 愛), simplified/traditional spellings, unknown characters become holders (龺), module answers the worst module, pinyin only on single-character strings (AssertionFailure), prints the traditional spelling, definitions come from HSKDictionaryLoader default registered with HSKString (cake, pastry), and an empty answer when the word is missing.
- HSKDomainTest, rest (7): HSKCharacterHolder structure with no-op traditional:/simplified:, H(龺) printing and neutral corpus selectors (hfwords/mdwords/graphicals/phonems empty Sets, frequency 4000, char-based <, = and hash); HSKCharacterProvider default singleton with detect:/select:, detect: errors and detect:ifNone: fallbacks, unknown characters memoized as holders, selects safe over a polluted corpus; HSKCharacterMarker assigns hsk1 to 我 and nohsk to unknowns; CharsetCategory instances (interval, allCharacters 256, UC(...) printing) and the parsed Unicode blocks (isBasicLatin, isLatin1Supplement).
- HSKAppTest (6): a fresh app has no users and a #simplified style; newUser creates, registers and selects an SRSUser whose goal characters are non-empty seeded from the corpus story (contains 我); users are chosen only from the registered list (Error otherwise); style changes announce HSKStyleChanged (isTraditional/isSimplified); user events announce HSKUserAdded and HSKUserSelected; domain notifications come from the current user announcer (SRSLevelUp on submitReview).
- HSKKnowledgeOverviewTest (4): an overview without a user offers nothing; entries equals the goal unlockedContent with unlocked/locked/total amounts; spellingOf: follows the app style (爱 vs 愛); levelOf:/nextReviewOf: reflect submitReview effects.
- HSKExercisePagesTest (10): HSKReminderPage starts on the current goal (SRSPhoneticExercise + HSKPhoneticTest), answers the current subject with its pinyin, registers failed answers keeping level 1, hints and gives up keeping level 1, navigates its queue without repeating the subject and counts progress (todo/done amounts). HSKQuizPage offers four options including its target, evaluates answers (identity) with review submission and level growth on success, advances without repeating its target and spells its target following the app style.
- HSKDesktopShellTest (8): the shell is a ToPane with header, knowledge, exercises, status, newUserButton and styleButton ids; no knowledge without a selected user; usersBar shows one entry per user and follows app announcements; knowledgeSpellingOf: follows the style; statusText updates on domain notifications; newUserButton and styleButton act through ToClickedSkinEvent (fired with fireEvent:).
- Gaps: SRSUser/SRSGoal end-to-end (SRSGoal has no characters setter; a successful session review triggers SRSUser levelup which breaks on a goal-less session); HSKCharacterProvider basicCharacters/children:/strictChildren: (instances never initialized); HSKCharacter phoneticFamily (sends the undefined HSKCharacter class>>instances) and radicalDistanceTo:; CharsetCategory latin1 and categoryFor: (undeclared Latin1 global); CEDICT file loading registers String keys that HSKString queries cannot match; HSKCharacterCrawl and the Spec UI.
- Runtime costs: user creation seeds the dictionary and streams the 小王子 story as an HSKString (about 0.7 s); reset the loader in tearDown of tests touching it.
- Run: SRSTestCase suite run; HSKAppTest suite run; HSKKnowledgeOverviewTest suite run; HSKExercisePagesTest suite run; HSKDesktopShellTest suite run; HSKDomainTest suite run; HSKTestTrie suite run; LZIHskObjectiveTest suite run; LZIReviewCharacterAssertionRule suite run.'